@@ -0,0 +1,80 @@
+# Deadline completion review packet
+
+The unit refuses successful logical results that finish after an applicable absolute
+deadline. Physical calls retain their actual success/failure, usage, latency and
+unknown/null accounting. It makes no socket cancellation claim. No live model call,
+browser, secret read, new dependency, default/resolver change or contract edit.
+
+Base: ac1efde173d4dc1d5fe8259f30888655a0072f08. Production: deabe55a27a2baca2f2929761b245de7e16f0b61.
+Final source/test: 46c44842af2131ac9f3bae716c7d5a2270e97177. Final proof specification/harness seal:
+2bd305c6207599810268e6c54351f06b38356b57. The wrapper candidate is recorded in the manifest.
+
+## Exact mechanism and immediate consumers
+
+`attempts.check_deadline` checks every enclosing scope and an optional immutable
+physical anchor. `now >= deadline` is terminal. Normal context exit checks completion;
+propagating privacy/validation exceptions stay unchanged. Call counts remain admission
+controls: a final allowed call finishing in time succeeds. Safe deadline exceptions
+suppress ambient vendor traceback context without exposing its text.
+
+LiteLLM records the physical outcome before its post-response check. Late vendor
+failures become terminal deadline errors before availability classification; no
+fallback hop occurs. `_complete` privately returns `(message, anchored_deadline)`;
+only its two strict parse consumers unpack it. Initial and repaired answers check the
+same anchor after validation. Each direct repair retains its existing separate
+physical timeout; no new aggregate timeout or mutable provider state. Enclosing
+logical deadlines remain absolute across both calls. Overdue malformed responses
+stop before repair. Text and sanitized frame paths share these boundaries.
+
+Gemini checks after SDK response, strict validation and generic SDK failure, retaining
+existing physical transport receipts. Gemini upload/poll transport accounting is
+unchanged. Vision probing checks before granting capability and after evaluation/
+cleanup; an overdue result is inconclusive with no capability, attached to the safe
+deadline exception. These changes gate Provider text/frame consumers, bounded SDK
+media return and probe capability consumers before they receive successful output.
+
+## Evidence and finite risks
+
+`final/environment.json`, `readiness.json` and `preflight.log` bind a fresh complete
+cache-free src/tests/scripts copy (including tests_mutation_fixtures), own-source
+imports, Python/dependencies, fixtures/config/lock, source/test and sealed spec/harness.
+`final/spec.json` defines exactly14 distinct timing/failure risks, grouped A6/B2/C6.
+Each final receipt binds command/output and before/after source hashes, one unique
+mutation, named defending failure, exact raw restoration and restored green. Group C
+includes bound final changed-file Ruff. Review the completed group receipts/bindings;
+readiness alone does not assert any executed proof. All14 final guard proofs are now
+complete: A12-case baseline/restored, B7-case baseline/restored and C9-case baseline/
+restored are green; each mutation has named red and exact restored green. Bound final
+Ruff is green. `final/final-summary.json` authenticates all35 phases and output hashes,
+with final source/test byte identity to46c44842. `design-caps.json` records line counts
+82/300/240/154 and functions<=50. These are separate focused group runs, not28 unique
+tests or a fabricated combined command.
+
+A covers exact edge, expired outer scope, successful scope exit, physical success
+before malformed repair, failed transport terminality and traceback suppression.
+B covers first/repair strict parsed return using direct/enclosing fake-clock cases.
+C covers SDK response/validation/failure and probe pregrant/completion/invalidation.
+Positive controls preserve the final allowed call, direct repair timeout policy and
+original privacy/validation errors. No broader provider/full-suite rerun is claimed.
+
+Earlier development receipts remain historical: initial20 at8b330790, safe-context9
+at10abf59e, parsed-return7 atdeabe55a. `final/historical-reuse.json` authenticates their
+recorded source/environment/lock and exact unchanged function ASTs; changed functions
+are listed explicitly and receive final focused proofs. There is no synthesized
+same-SHA combined run. The two existing test arrangements move `pytest.raises` outside
+the whole budget scope so terminal expiry is asserted at the full scope boundary;
+they do not suppress expiry then accidentally demand a successful context exit.
+
+## Review focus and limits
+
+C5/C9/C12 and D101/D102: no vendor payload in errors, actual declared deadline controls,
+truthful physical records and terminal global expiry. Check that validation time is
+inside completion, expired output cannot become capability/fallback, original errors
+survive and count exhaustion is not a post-call rejection. Check both private tuple
+consumers and immutable anchor identity. Functions remain<=50 lines; changed providers
+remain<=300. Existing media socket deadlines/retry policy and model choices are not
+expanded. No hard-cancel guarantee, aggregate direct repair cap or whole-repo acceptance.
+
+Whole-maker active seconds/tokens/cost are unknown/null. Recorded command durations
+are subprocess wall time only. Reviewer efficiency is a target, not a measured claim.
+Only an independent checker may issue PASS; no master merge/push is authorized here.
